{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/612443-request-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-merging-1ed-and-2ed-gifts","id":612443,"title":"Request for advice on how to deal with merging 1ed and 2ed gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-02T11:45:49-07:00","id":612443,"title":"Request for advice on how to deal with merging 1ed and 2ed gifts","content":"I am playing in my first WtF game ever. I ran many games of 1ed since it first game out, but never had a GM. Now, my friend is GMing for her first time, and we are all playing 2ed. We finished our first chapter yesterday and had our Rahu really break the game imo.<br /> <br /> He convinced our GM, really he just asked if he could and she said yes, to let him purchase 2 dots in Purity. This was my first mistake, I should have spoken up and said the rules are very hazy as to whether or not he should be allowed to purchase 2 dots at once. He then asked her if he could take a 4 dot gift from 1ed and she allowed him to. Again, I should have spoken up but we were among friends, I was busy doing my own leveling, and didn't want to sound like a rule jerk. As a result, our Rahu now has Father Wolf's Savage Rending. He bought a gift that would have cost over 30 points in renown in 1ed for just 6 points.<br /> <br /> Now, we nerfed it pretty hard. We decided that each attack can only do, at most, levels of agg equal to his dots in Purity. After a short talk, one where I felt very awkward cause it was obvious I was the only one who thought this might not be acceptable, the group decided to accept this. The problem, I think, is even bigger because he will be comboing this ability with several of the really good abilities in 2ed, such as 8 agains, Efficient Killer, Primal Stength, all the Full Moon gifts he has for 4 ranks in Purity, and the use of a very good Irraka who will be making sure to deny many people their defenses. <br /> <br /> My real concern isn't jealousy, it's more that as a seasoned GM I really am not able to see how this character will be challenged in combat without throwing something that will easily one-shot the other two wolves in our pack. I also have completely lost interest in ever trying to get any gift or ability that will give me usefulness in combat. Already, we are a 3 pack group with troubles, we have a Rahu and an Irraka only focusing on combat and I am having to pull up the slack for everything else. That is what it is, our face and our Gibbous had to drop out before we even started playing for personal reasons. I am just afraid that, as much as WoD has focus outside of combat, the combats we have will not be much of anything for the other two of us in the pack, well, outside of just denying opponents their Defense for the Irraka. Or, like I said, the we will just be liabilities due to the level of what it will take to challenge the Rahu.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? I could be completely over-reacting. When I had no idea what I was talking about looking at the 2e rules I got some great, and accurate btw, feedback here so I am seeking wisdom again. If you do think that there is an issue with what is on the table, how would you handle it? I hate to be the fun police and I am not the GM so I don't want to overstep my boundaries and be that guy. Thanks everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T14:14:35-07:00","id":612593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/612443-request-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-merging-1ed-and-2ed-gifts#post612443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am playing in my first WtF game ever. I ran many games of 1ed since it first game out, but never had a GM. Now, my friend is GMing for her first time, and we are all playing 2ed. We finished our first chapter yesterday and had our Rahu really break the game imo.<br /> <br /> He convinced our GM, really he just asked if he could and she said yes, to let him purchase 2 dots in Purity. This was my first mistake, I should have spoken up and said the rules are very hazy as to whether or not he should be allowed to purchase 2 dots at once.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see any problem with that. Technically he should probably have needed to do multiple Purity-worthy deeds to get multiple dots of Purity, but some STs are more lenient on story justifications for XP purchases and that's ok. By itself, I don't see this causing any problems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/612443-request-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-merging-1ed-and-2ed-gifts#post612443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He then asked her if he could take a 4 dot gift from 1ed and she allowed him to. Again, I should have spoken up but we were among friends, I was busy doing my own leveling, and didn't want to sound like a rule jerk. As a result, our Rahu now has Father Wolf's Savage Rending. He bought a gift that would have cost over 30 points in renown in 1ed for just 6 points.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is an odd choice. I wouldn't want to mix systems like that if it were my game, especially since Gifts work so differently now than they did in 1e. That said, experiences in 2e are worth more than experience points were in 1e. Each beat in 2e is roughly the equivalent of 1 experience point in 1e, so 6 experiences <i>would</i> be worth about 30 old xp. So by that logic it checks out (kind of).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/612443-request-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-merging-1ed-and-2ed-gifts#post612443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, we nerfed it pretty hard. We decided that each attack can only do, at most, levels of agg equal to his dots in Purity. After a short talk, one where I felt very awkward cause it was obvious I was the only one who thought this might not be acceptable, the group decided to accept this. The problem, I think, is even bigger because he will be comboing this ability with several of the really good abilities in 2ed, such as 8 agains, Efficient Killer, Primal Stength, all the Full Moon gifts he has for 4 ranks in Purity, and the use of a very good Irraka who will be making sure to deny many people their defenses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, that just sounds like a character being good at what he's built for to me. And if you're the only one who has reservations about it, maybe just let them try it out. You may be pleasantly surprised. Or, it may turn out to cause huge problems. Worst case scenario, if the group agrees it's causing problems, you just do a minor character re-write, and it's a learning experience.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Face_Plont</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/612443-request-for-advice-on-how-to-deal-with-merging-1ed-and-2ed-gifts#post612443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My real concern isn't jealousy, it's more that as a seasoned GM I really am not able to see how this character will be challenged in combat without throwing something that will easily one-shot the other two wolves in our pack. I also have completely lost interest in ever trying to get any gift or ability that will give me usefulness in combat. Already, we are a 3 pack group with troubles, we have a Rahu and an Irraka only focusing on combat and I am having to pull up the slack for everything else. That is what it is, our face and our Gibbous had to drop out before we even started playing for personal reasons. I am just afraid that, as much as WoD has focus outside of combat, the combats we have will not be much of anything for the other two of us in the pack, well, outside of just denying opponents their Defense for the Irraka. Or, like I said, the we will just be liabilities due to the level of what it will take to challenge the Rahu.<br /> <br /> What do you guys think? I could be completely over-reacting. When I had no idea what I was talking about looking at the 2e rules I got some great, and accurate btw, feedback here so I am seeking wisdom again. If you do think that there is an issue with what is on the table, how would you handle it? I hate to be the fun police and I am not the GM so I don't want to overstep my boundaries and be that guy. Thanks everyone <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't worry too much. 2e is very much not afraid to let characters be awesome at the thing they're specialized in. If you build a combat wombat, it <i>should</i> be hard for the ST to challenge you with a head-on physical confrontation. Instead, they should try to challenge you by taking your character out of her element. Sure, you can rip any Azlu to pieces, but when a conspiracy of humans starts using their sociopolitical power to make your territory totally unlivable for you, no amount of damage is going to rip through that red tape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T17:41:33-07:00","id":612847,"title":"","content":"I would say he's definitely taking advantage of the rules but it doesn't break the game at all. Especially since you can do the same thing if you'd like for the higher rank abilities which are honestly going to end up being much more useful than Savage Rending. Honestly, aggravated isn't as big a deal as the game makes it out to be except where player characters are concerned. You die when you're filled up with lethal just as hard as you die from being filled with agg. I mean, the fact that most creatures don't regenerate agg is a factor, but most baddies aren't relying on regeneration (except other uratha) to be bad. And armor does the same thing. Armor blocks aggravated damage first, so 3 points of armor blocks most of this guy's damage.<br /> <br /> More importantly, the Rahu is supposed to eclipse everyone else in damage. The Irraka in assassination. You do what what you are good at and focus on that, I promise you'll be even more useful because of their complete specialization in one area. I think your Rahu being a super effective Rahu is only going to make your job easier.<br /> <br /> Our house rules for gifts were that each gift costed the same as its level. So a rank 4 gift would cost 4 experience, provided you had renown at 4. It's clunky and yeah, does mess with balance a bit. But if you insist on having them in the game, it's a way to do it. Remember that vampires get aggravated damage at promethean 4 with a merit, I believe, and they are doing fine with balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:10:44-07:00","id":612896,"title":"","content":"Protean 4, while in Frenzy with a Merit. Promethean 4 did make me laugh a little bit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":11,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","user":"Darksider","date":". 08-05-2015, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-02T19:24:30-07:00","id":612901,"title":"","content":"Haha, I knew that. My bad. Should have proofread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-04T17:22:40-07:00","id":615784,"title":"","content":"Again, thanks everyone, I figured it was going to be alright. I really don't feel bad now because we are playing a Vegas campaign and the GM has made it clear the real problem with our territory currently is the corrupt coven of vamps in charge. Knowing that they will have a 4 dot agg gift to throw at us makes the difference. I also am not complaining about the Rahu focusing on damage, I get that is their job.<br /> <br /> Thanks for all your thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1883-face_plont","name":"Face_Plont","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1883_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-05T09:34:19-07:00","id":616586,"title":"","content":"Yeah no, it's a valid balance concern, but it should be fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6422-lionel","name":"Lionel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6422_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}